{"schema":"plectis_maths_universe_excerpts_v2","paper":"erdos249-totient-reasoning-surface","excerpts":[["statement:erdos249-totient-reasoning-surface#prop:b5","Information lost by specific carry\ndescriptions","<p><em></em></p>\n<ol>\n<li><p><em>Fix <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>m</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>2</mn></math></span> and write\n<span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>R</mi><mo>=</mo><mo fence=\"false\" stretchy=\"false\">⌊</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn><mo fence=\"false\" stretchy=\"false\">⌋</mo></math></span>. For <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>…</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>R</mi></math></span>, let <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></math></span> vanish except at <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>R</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>r</mi></math></span> and <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>r</mi></math></span>. Each sequence satisfies\n<span class=\"math inline\"><math><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>≤</mo><mi>n</mi></math></span>, has the same\nbinary sum <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>R</mi><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msup></math></span>, and has the\nsame coefficients and scaled tails before position <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>m</mi></math></span>. Its scaled tail at position <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>m</mi></math></span> is <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>r</mi></math></span>. The common history therefore does not\ndetermine that tail. A finite set of labels that determines the tail for\neach member of this family must contain at least <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>R</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>=</mo><mo fence=\"false\" stretchy=\"false\">⌊</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn><mo fence=\"false\" stretchy=\"false\">⌋</mo><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></math></span> elements, one\nfor each value of <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>r</mi></math></span>.</em></p></li>\n<li><p><em>Reduction modulo <span class=\"math inline\"><math><msup><mn>2</mn><mi>L</mi></msup></math></span>\nforgets the initial value after the same <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>L</mi></math></span> recurrence steps: two affine binary\norbits with different seeds satisfy <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><msub><mrow><mi>orbit</mi></mrow><mi>u</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>−</mo><msub><mrow><mi>orbit</mi></mrow><mi>v</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi>L</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></math></span>, so the endpoint residue mod <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi>L</mi></mrow></msup></math></span> is independent of the initial\ncarry.</em></p></li>\n<li><p><em>Fix a precision <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>u</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></math></span>, a\nfinite list of nonnegative valuations <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><msub><mi>ν</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></math></span> and odd integers <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></math></span>, and an initial integer <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><msub><mi>e</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></math></span>. There are integers <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></math></span> such that </em></p>\n<div class=\"math-display\"><span\nclass=\"math display\"><math display=\"block\"><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><msub><mi>ν</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mi>u</mi></msup><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>,</mo><mspace width=\"2em\"></mspace><msub><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mspace width=\"2em\"></mspace><mo stretchy=\"false\">|</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">|</mo><mo>≤</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><msub><mi>ν</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>.</mo></math></span></div>\n<p><em> At each\nstep, choose the centred representative of <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mn>2</mn><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><msub><mi>ν</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></msup><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></math></span> modulo <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><msub><mi>ν</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></msup></math></span>. The unrestricted integers\n<span class=\"math inline\"><math><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></math></span> are essential: the assertion\ndoes not prescribe the full coefficients <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></math></span>.</em></p></li>\n</ol>\n<p><em>These statements exclude decoders using only the specified common\nhistory, distinctions using only the endpoint residue, and\ncontradictions using only the stated local symbols. They do not prove\nthat the actual totient expansion cannot be studied by automata. A\nproposed application must verify that it uses no additional arithmetic\ninformation that the comparison families fail to preserve.</em></p>"],["statement:erdos249-totient-reasoning-surface#prop:b6","Four limits of particular linear\nconstructions","<p><em> The following four constructions have different\nlimitations. They must not be read as a claim that every finite family\nof totient sections is independent: the full family has the explicit\nrelations described in the short paper.</em></p>\n<ol>\n<li><p><em><em>Dyadic sections and an integer identity.</em> The\nretained family of <span class=\"math inline\"><math><msup><mn>2</mn><mi>e</mi></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></math></span> dyadic\nsections is linearly independent over <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mrow><mi>ℚ</mi></mrow></math></span> for <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>e</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></math></span> (Proposition <a class=\"math-ref\" href=\"papers/erdos249-totient-reasoning-surface.html#prop:rank\" data-universe-ref=\"statement:erdos249-totient-reasoning-surface#prop:rank\">1.6</a>). Separately, positive\nintegers <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>Q</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi></math></span> and integers <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi></math></span> cannot satisfy </em></p>\n<div class=\"math-display\"><span\nclass=\"math display\"><math display=\"block\"><mi>A</mi><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mspace width=\"2em\"></mspace><mi>Q</mi><mi>v</mi><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>,</mo><mspace width=\"2em\"></mspace><mo stretchy=\"false\">|</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">|</mo><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>Q</mi><mi>v</mi><mo>,</mo></math></span></div>\n<p class=\"display-continue\"><em>\nbecause <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mo stretchy=\"false\">|</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">|</mo><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></math></span> gives <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mo stretchy=\"false\">|</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">|</mo><mo>≥</mo><mi>Q</mi><mi>v</mi></math></span>. This elementary\nincompatibility concerns the displayed requirements; it does not exclude\nevery argument using an adjugate matrix.</em></p></li>\n<li><p><em><em>Möbius incidence.</em> <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo>+</mo></mrow><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>/</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mrow><mo>+</mo></mrow><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></math></span> when\n<span class=\"math inline\"><math><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mrow><mo>+</mo></mrow><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>∣</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo>+</mo></mrow><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></math></span> and <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mn>0</mn></math></span> otherwise is lower triangular with unit\ndiagonal, so <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mo movablelimits=\"true\">det</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math></span> for every\n<span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>N</mi></math></span>. Hence multiplication by <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>N</mi></msub></math></span> is injective; the corresponding\ncoefficient transformation cannot create a nonzero vector in its\nkernel.</em></p></li>\n<li><p><em><em>Adjugate reconstruction.</em> Let <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>ℚ</mi></mrow></math></span> and <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>ℕ</mi></mrow></math></span> be finite families with\n<span class=\"math inline\"><math><munder><mo>∑</mo><mi>i</mi></munder><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mi>φ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math></span>.\nReconstructing each value from two tails and bounding them separately\ngives the error bound <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><munder><mo>∑</mo><mi>i</mi></munder><mo stretchy=\"false\">|</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">|</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mn>3</mn><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></math></span>. It is at least <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mn>3</mn></math></span>, since </em></p>\n<div class=\"math-display\"><span\nclass=\"math display\"><math display=\"block\"><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><munder><mo>∑</mo><mi>i</mi></munder><mo stretchy=\"false\">|</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">|</mo><mi>φ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>≤</mo><munder><mo>∑</mo><mi>i</mi></munder><mo stretchy=\"false\">|</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">|</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>.</mo></math></span></div>\n<p><em>\nConsequently this particular bound cannot be less than <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mn>1</mn></math></span>, whatever the size of the evaluation\nmatrix.</em></p></li>\n<li><p><em><em>Finite combinations of shifts.</em> The synthetic\nsequence in Observation <a class=\"math-ref\" href=\"papers/erdos249-totient-reasoning-surface.html#prop:B4b-kill\">6.115</a> has the prescribed\ndifferences <span class=\"math inline\"><math><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mi>H</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>φ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></math></span>\nfor <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mn>2</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi></math></span>, where <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>H</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>lcm</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>…</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></math></span>. It is\nof the form <span class=\"math inline\"><math><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></math></span>, and\nevery finite integer combination of its shifts has the same form with a\ncorrespondingly shifted state. Thus these linear operations alone do not\nremove the compatible carry recurrence. Their uniform bounds depend on\nthe absolute coefficient sum, as made explicit in that observation. The\nconstruction does not assert that <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></math></span> equals the actual totient difference\nat other indices.</em></p></li>\n</ol>\n<p><em>A further limitation concerns quotients of the finite sums <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><munderover><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>Y</mi></mrow></munderover><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>/</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mi>d</mi></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mi>r</mi></msup></math></span>.\nFor <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>e</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></math></span> and <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>Y</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>4</mn></math></span>, </em></p>\n<div class=\"math-display\"><span\nclass=\"math display\"><math display=\"block\"><mfrac><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>e</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>e</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo>−</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>S</mi><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle=\"false\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>&gt;</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>480</mn></mfrac><mo>.</mo></math></span></div>\n<p><em>\nThe proof bounds each infinite sum <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><munder><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munder><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>/</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mi>d</mi></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mi>r</mi></msup></math></span>, <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>r</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>3</mn></math></span>, between <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mn>1429</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>1512</mn></math></span> and <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mn>1</mn></math></span>, and its truncation error after <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>Y</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>4</mn></math></span> terms by <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>3584</mn></math></span>. Thus the lower bound holds for\nevery stated pair <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>e</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Y</mi></math></span>, not just a\nfinite list of computed examples. These results concern the listed\nmatrices, estimates, and comparison sequence. The fourth item has the\nexplicit construction and source theorem given in Observation <a class=\"math-ref\" href=\"papers/erdos249-totient-reasoning-surface.html#prop:B4b-kill\">6.115</a>. A different\nfinite-dimensional argument, or one using further arithmetic\nassumptions, is not excluded. Proposition <a class=\"math-ref\" href=\"papers/erdos249-totient-reasoning-surface.html#prop:period-not-rank\" data-universe-ref=\"statement:erdos249-totient-reasoning-surface#prop:period-not-rank\">1.7</a> is conditional\non rationality of <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>S</mi></math></span> and is not, by\nitself, a counterexample. The separate rational <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mn>5</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>4</mn></math></span> comparison supplies the\ncounterexample to the generic rank bound.</em></p>"],["statement:erdos249-totient-reasoning-surface#prop:b7","The coefficient properties of the\nrational example","<p><em> The rational sequence in Proposition <a class=\"math-ref\" href=\"papers/erdos249-totient-reasoning-surface.html#prop:parity\" data-universe-ref=\"statement:erdos249-totient-reasoning-surface#prop:parity\">1.9</a> satisfies uniform\nboundedness, <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>≤</mo><mi>n</mi></math></span>, agreement\nwith <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>φ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></math></span> modulo <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mn>2</mn></math></span> at every index, and the stated\nseparated-carry form of aperiodicity. Consequently, those properties\nalone cannot imply irrationality of a dyadic series. The example does\nnot exclude arguments using further totient identities, including its\nmultiplicative relations.</em></p>"],["statement:erdos249-totient-reasoning-surface#thm:goodbasegap","Irrationality from one bound on the good\nindices","<p><em></em></p>\n<ol>\n<li><p><em>Suppose that for every <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>h</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></math></span> and every <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>A</mi></math></span> there are <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>X</mi></math></span>, <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>L</mi></math></span>\nwith <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mn>16</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>X</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>h</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>L</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>≤</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mi>L</mi></msup></math></span> and a\nnonempty finite set <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>T</mi></math></span> of integers\nin <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mo stretchy=\"false\">[</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></math></span> with </em></p>\n<div class=\"math-display\"><span\nclass=\"math display\"><math display=\"block\"><munder><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></munder><mi>Re</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mi>E</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>h</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>N</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>≤</mo><mstyle displaystyle=\"false\"><mfrac><mn>9</mn><mn>10</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mspace width=\"0.167em\"></mspace><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">#</mi><mi>T</mi><mo>.</mo></math></span></div>\n<p><em> Then <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>S</mi><mo>∉</mo><mrow><mi>ℚ</mi></mrow></math></span> (<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/wcook04/plectis-erdos/blob/24edbddbe2bd68e920327a701aad0b9dd0d69675/lean/ErdosProblems/ArgumentGraph/Results/Erdos249Endpoint.lean#L44\" data-link-kind=\"exogenous\" rel=\"external noopener\"><code>irrational_totient_series_of_support_gap</code></a>).</em></p></li>\n<li><p><em>Take <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>s</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>26</mn></math></span>, <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>η</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>1000</mn></math></span> and <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>L</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></math></span>. Suppose that for every <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>h</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></math></span> there are arbitrarily large <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>X</mi></math></span> with </em></p>\n<div class=\"math-display\"><span\nclass=\"math display\"><math display=\"block\"><mi>Re</mi><mo>⁡</mo><munder><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>𝒢</mi></mrow></mrow></munder><mi>E</mi><mrow><mo minsize=\"1.2em\" maxsize=\"1.2em\">(</mo></mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>N</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mrow><mo minsize=\"1.2em\" maxsize=\"1.2em\">)</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mstyle displaystyle=\"false\"><mfrac><mn>603</mn><mn>1000</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mi>X</mi><mo>.</mo></math></span></div>\n<p><em> Then <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>S</mi><mo>∉</mo><mrow><mi>ℚ</mi></mrow></math></span> (<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/wcook04/plectis-erdos/blob/24edbddbe2bd68e920327a701aad0b9dd0d69675/lean/ErdosProblems/ArgumentGraph/Results/Erdos249Endpoint.lean#L100\" data-link-kind=\"exogenous\" rel=\"external noopener\"><code>irrational_totient_series_of_goodBase_gap</code></a>).</em></p></li>\n</ol>"],["statement:erdos249-totient-reasoning-surface#prop:shift","Digit-shift identity","<p><em> For\nevery <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>N</mi><mo>:</mo><mrow><mi>ℕ</mi></mrow></math></span>, </em></p>\n<div class=\"math-display\"><span\nclass=\"math display\"><math display=\"block\"><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi>N</mi></mrow></msup><mo>⋅</mo><mi>S</mi><mspace width=\"0.278em\"></mspace><mo>=</mo><mspace width=\"0.278em\"></mspace><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Φ</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo>,</mo></math></span></div>\n<p class=\"display-continue\"><em> where\n<span class=\"math inline\"><math><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Φ</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><munder><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></munder><mi>φ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>⋅</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msup><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>ℕ</mi></mrow></math></span> (the integer prefix) and <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><munder><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></munder><mi>φ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>N</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>/</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math></span> (the scaled tail, <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mrow><mi>R</mi></mrow></math></span> in Lean).</em></p>"],["statement:erdos249-totient-reasoning-surface#lem:farey","Farey gap, fully general","<p><em> For\nintegers <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi></math></span> with <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>b</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></math></span>, <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>d</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></math></span>, <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>b</mi><mi>c</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>a</mi><mi>d</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math></span> (i.e. <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>a</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>b</mi></math></span> and <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>c</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>d</mi></math></span> are unimodular Farey neighbours), and\n<span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>a</mi><mi>s</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>r</mi><mi>b</mi></math></span>, <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>r</mi><mi>d</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>c</mi><mi>s</mi></math></span> (i.e. <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>r</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>s</mi></math></span> lies strictly between them): <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>b</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>s</mi></math></span>.</em></p>"],["statement:erdos249-totient-reasoning-surface#prop:gapwindow","The Farey certificate at <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>K</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>240</mn></math></span>","<p><em> For the window <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>N</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>240</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></math></span>, put </em></p>\n<div class=\"math-display\"><span\nclass=\"math display\"><math display=\"block\"><mi>V</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><munderover><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>240</mn></mrow></munderover><mi>φ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mn>240</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace=\"0.278em\" rspace=\"0.278em\">mod</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mn>240</mn></mrow></msup><mo>.</mo></math></span></div>\n<p><em>\nFor every <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>q</mi><mo>:</mo><mrow><mi>ℕ</mi></mrow></math></span> with </em></p>\n<div class=\"math-display\"><span\nclass=\"math display\"><math display=\"block\"><mn>0</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>q</mi><mspace width=\"0.278em\"></mspace><mo>≤</mo><mspace width=\"0.278em\"></mspace><msub><mi>Q</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>:=</mo><mn>79</mn><mspace width=\"0.167em\"></mspace><mn>639</mn><mspace width=\"0.167em\"></mspace><mn>646</mn><mspace width=\"0.167em\"></mspace><mn>646</mn><mspace width=\"0.167em\"></mspace><mn>701</mn><mspace width=\"0.167em\"></mspace><mn>375</mn><mspace width=\"0.167em\"></mspace><mn>323</mn><mspace width=\"0.167em\"></mspace><mn>355</mn><mspace width=\"0.167em\"></mspace><mn>774</mn><mspace width=\"0.167em\"></mspace><mn>875</mn><mspace width=\"0.167em\"></mspace><mn>831</mn><mspace width=\"0.167em\"></mspace><mn>053</mn><mspace width=\"0.278em\"></mspace><mspace width=\"0.278em\"></mspace><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mo>≈</mo><mn>7.96</mn><mo>×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mn>34</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>,</mo></math></span></div>\n<div class=\"math-display\"><span class=\"math display\"><math display=\"block\"><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>⋅</mo><mi>V</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo lspace=\"0.278em\" rspace=\"0.278em\">mod</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mn>240</mn></mrow></msup><mspace width=\"0.278em\"></mspace><mo>+</mo><mspace width=\"0.278em\"></mspace><mn>243</mn><mspace width=\"0.167em\"></mspace><mi>q</mi><mspace width=\"0.278em\"></mspace><mo>&lt;</mo><mspace width=\"0.278em\"></mspace><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mn>240</mn></mrow></msup><mo>.</mo></math></span></div>\n<p><em> This bound is\n<em>sharp</em>: <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>q</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>79</mn><mspace width=\"0.167em\"></mspace><mn>639</mn><mspace width=\"0.167em\"></mspace><mn>646</mn><mspace width=\"0.167em\"></mspace><mn>646</mn><mspace width=\"0.167em\"></mspace><mn>701</mn><mspace width=\"0.167em\"></mspace><mn>375</mn><mspace width=\"0.167em\"></mspace><mn>323</mn><mspace width=\"0.167em\"></mspace><mn>355</mn><mspace width=\"0.167em\"></mspace><mn>774</mn><mspace width=\"0.167em\"></mspace><mn>875</mn><mspace width=\"0.167em\"></mspace><mn>831</mn><mspace width=\"0.167em\"></mspace><mn>054</mn></math></span> is\nthe exact first failing denominator, obtained as the denominator of the\nmediant of two explicit unimodular Farey neighbours.</em></p>"],["statement:erdos249-totient-reasoning-surface#thm:denom-record","Denominator exclusion","<p><em> For every\n<span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>p</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>ℚ</mi></mrow></math></span> whose reduced\ndenominator is at most <span class=\"math inline\"><math><msub><mi>Q</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></math></span>, </em></p>\n<div class=\"math-display\"><span\nclass=\"math display\"><math display=\"block\"><mi>S</mi><mspace width=\"0.278em\"></mspace><mo>≠</mo><mspace width=\"0.278em\"></mspace><mi>p</mi><mo>.</mo></math></span></div>\n<p><em> Equivalently: <em>if <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>S</mi></math></span> is rational, its reduced denominator\nexceeds</em> <span class=\"math inline\"><math><msub><mi>Q</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>≈</mo><mn>7.96</mn><mo>×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mn>34</mn></mrow></msup></math></span>.</em></p>"],["statement:erdos249-totient-reasoning-surface#prop:coprime","Fair-coin coprimality form","<p><em>\nLet <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Y</mi></math></span> be independent random\nvariables with <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mo movablelimits=\"true\">Pr</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mo movablelimits=\"true\">Pr</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msup></math></span> for <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>n</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></math></span> (independent fair-coin waiting\ntimes). Then </em></p>\n<div class=\"math-display\"><span class=\"math display\"><math display=\"block\"><mi>S</mi><mspace width=\"0.278em\"></mspace><mo>=</mo><mspace width=\"0.278em\"></mspace><mstyle displaystyle=\"false\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mspace width=\"0.278em\"></mspace><mo>+</mo><mspace width=\"0.278em\"></mspace><mo movablelimits=\"true\">Pr</mo><mrow><mo minsize=\"1.2em\" maxsize=\"1.2em\">(</mo></mrow><mo movablelimits=\"true\">gcd</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo minsize=\"1.2em\" maxsize=\"1.2em\">)</mo></mrow><mspace width=\"0.278em\"></mspace><mo>=</mo><mspace width=\"0.278em\"></mspace><mstyle displaystyle=\"false\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mspace width=\"0.278em\"></mspace><mo>+</mo><mspace width=\"0.278em\"></mspace><munder><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mtable columnspacing=\"0em\" rowspacing=\"0.1em\"><mtr><mtd><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mo movablelimits=\"true\">gcd</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></munder><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>.</mo></math></span></div>\n<p><em> Equivalently, on the visible lattice: summing <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow></msup></math></span> over the half-open coprime\npairs (<span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>a</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></math></span>, <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>b</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></math></span>, <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mo movablelimits=\"true\">gcd</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math></span>) recovers <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><munder><mo>∑</mo><mi>n</mi></munder><mi>φ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>/</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mi>n</mi></msup></math></span> exactly, with no\nboundary correction, because the visible-point count on the half-open\nantidiagonal at height <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>n</mi></math></span> equals\n<span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>φ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></math></span> for every <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>n</mi></math></span>, including <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></math></span>.</em></p>"],["statement:erdos249-totient-reasoning-surface#prop:gcdlayer","The gcd-layer normalisation","<p><em>\nFor independent fair-coin waiting times as above, <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><munder><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munder><mo movablelimits=\"true\">Pr</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mo movablelimits=\"true\">gcd</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math></span> exactly;\nand for every <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>d</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></math></span>, <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mo movablelimits=\"true\">Pr</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>∣</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>∧</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>∣</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mi>d</mi></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mn>2</mn></msup></math></span>.</em></p>"],["statement:erdos249-totient-reasoning-surface#thm:denomcoprime","Denominator exclusion for the\ncoprimality-probability form","<p><em> Let </em></p>\n<div class=\"math-display\"><span class=\"math display\"><math display=\"block\"><msub><mi>Q</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo>⌊</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>Q</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>⌋</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>39</mn><mspace width=\"0.167em\"></mspace><mn>819</mn><mspace width=\"0.167em\"></mspace><mn>823</mn><mspace width=\"0.167em\"></mspace><mn>323</mn><mspace width=\"0.167em\"></mspace><mn>350</mn><mspace width=\"0.167em\"></mspace><mn>687</mn><mspace width=\"0.167em\"></mspace><mn>661</mn><mspace width=\"0.167em\"></mspace><mn>677</mn><mspace width=\"0.167em\"></mspace><mn>887</mn><mspace width=\"0.167em\"></mspace><mn>437</mn><mspace width=\"0.167em\"></mspace><mn>915</mn><mspace width=\"0.167em\"></mspace><mn>526.</mn></math></span></div>\n<p><em> For\nevery <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>a</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>ℤ</mi></mrow></math></span>, <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>d</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>ℕ</mi></mrow></math></span> with <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mn>0</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math></span>: the visible coprime-pair\nprobability <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mo movablelimits=\"true\">Pr</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mo movablelimits=\"true\">gcd</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></math></span> is not\nequal to <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>a</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>d</mi></math></span>.</em></p>"],["statement:erdos249-totient-reasoning-surface#thm:denommobsq","Denominator exclusion for the\nMöbius-square form","<p><em> With <span class=\"math inline\"><math><msub><mi>Q</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math></span>\nas in Theorem <a class=\"math-ref\" href=\"papers/erdos249-totient-reasoning-surface.html#thm:denomcoprime\" data-universe-ref=\"statement:erdos249-totient-reasoning-surface#thm:denomcoprime\">5.11</a>: for every <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>a</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>ℤ</mi></mrow></math></span>, <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>d</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>ℕ</mi></mrow></math></span> with <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mn>0</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math></span>, the signed series <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>T</mi><mo>:=</mo><munder><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munder><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>/</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mi>m</mi></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mi>S</mi><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math></span> (see §<a class=\"math-ref\" href=\"papers/erdos249-totient-reasoning-surface.html#ssec:mobius\">5.5</a>) is not equal to <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>a</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>d</mi></math></span>.</em></p>"],["statement:erdos249-totient-reasoning-surface#prop:mobsq","Möbius-square reduction","<p><em> </em></p>\n<div class=\"math-display\"><span\nclass=\"math display\"><math display=\"block\"><mi>S</mi><mspace width=\"0.278em\"></mspace><mo>=</mo><mspace width=\"0.278em\"></mspace><munder><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munder><mfrac><mrow><mi>φ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow><msup><mn>2</mn><mi>n</mi></msup></mfrac><mspace width=\"0.278em\"></mspace><mo>=</mo><mspace width=\"0.278em\"></mspace><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mspace width=\"0.278em\"></mspace><mo>+</mo><mspace width=\"0.278em\"></mspace><munder><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munder><mfrac><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mi>d</mi></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo>,</mo></math></span></div>\n<p class=\"display-continue\"><em> where <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>μ</mi></math></span> is the Möbius function, so <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>∈</mo><mo fence=\"false\" stretchy=\"false\">{</mo><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo fence=\"false\" stretchy=\"false\">}</mo></math></span> for every <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>d</mi></math></span>. Consequently <em>Erdős #249 <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mspace width=\"0.278em\"></mspace><mo stretchy=\"false\">⟺</mo><mspace width=\"0.278em\"></mspace></math></span> <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>T</mi><mo>:=</mo><munder><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munder><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>/</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mi>d</mi></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>∉</mo><mrow><mi>ℚ</mi></mrow></math></span></em>, since adding a rational number does not change\nirrationality.</em></p>"],["statement:erdos249-totient-reasoning-surface#prop:lambertengine","The squared-Lambert identity","<p><em>\nFor <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>w</mi><mo>:</mo><mrow><mi>ℕ</mi></mrow><mo accent=\"false\" stretchy=\"false\">→</mo><mrow><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow></math></span> with\n<span class=\"math inline\"><math><mo stretchy=\"false\">|</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">|</mo><mo>≤</mo><mi>d</mi></math></span> for all <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>d</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></math></span>, and <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>1</mn></math></span>: </em></p>\n<div class=\"math-display\"><span\nclass=\"math display\"><math display=\"block\"><munder><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munder><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>r</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mspace width=\"0.278em\"></mspace><mo>=</mo><mspace width=\"0.278em\"></mspace><munder><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munder><mrow><mo>(</mo><munder><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo>∣</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></munder><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mrow><mo minsize=\"1.623em\" maxsize=\"1.623em\">(</mo></mrow><mstyle displaystyle=\"false\"><mfrac><mi>n</mi><mi>e</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo minsize=\"1.623em\" maxsize=\"1.623em\">)</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mi>n</mi></msup><mo>.</mo></math></span></div>"],["statement:erdos249-totient-reasoning-surface#prop:zetaq","The divisor-sum identity","<p><em>\n</em></p>\n<div class=\"math-display\"><span class=\"math display\"><math display=\"block\"><munder><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munder><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mi>d</mi></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac><mspace width=\"0.278em\"></mspace><mo>=</mo><mspace width=\"0.278em\"></mspace><munder><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munder><mfrac><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>−</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow><msup><mn>2</mn><mi>n</mi></msup></mfrac><mspace width=\"0.278em\"></mspace><mo>=</mo><mspace width=\"0.278em\"></mspace><msub><mi>ζ</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ζ</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mtext> at </mtext><mi>q</mi><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle=\"false\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo>,</mo></math></span></div>\n<p class=\"display-continue\"><em> where <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>σ</mi></math></span> is the sum-of-divisors function\nand <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>τ</mi></math></span> the number-of-divisors\nfunction. The <em>identity</em> is machine-checked. With <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><msub><mi>ζ</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><munder><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munder><msup><mi>n</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><msup><mi>q</mi><mi>n</mi></msup><mo>/</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>q</mi><mi>n</mi></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></math></span>,\nPostelmans and Van Assche prove that <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>ζ</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>ζ</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></math></span> are linearly\nindependent over <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mrow><mi>ℚ</mi></mrow></math></span> for\n<span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>q</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>p</mi></math></span> with an integer <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>p</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>2</mn></math></span> <span class=\"citation\"\ndata-cites=\"postelmans-vanassche\"><a href=\"papers/erdos249-totient-reasoning-surface.html#ref-12\">[12]</a></span>; at <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>q</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math></span> this gives the irrationality\nof the <em>value</em> <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><msub><mi>ζ</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ζ</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></math></span>. Two irrational\nnumbers can have a rational difference, so the separate irrationality of\nthe two values would not suffice.</em></p>"],["statement:erdos249-totient-reasoning-surface#prop:pillai","The gcd-moment identity","<p><em> </em></p>\n<div class=\"math-display\"><span\nclass=\"math display\"><math display=\"block\"><munder><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munder><mfrac><mrow><mi>φ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mi>d</mi></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac><mspace width=\"0.278em\"></mspace><mo>=</mo><mspace width=\"0.278em\"></mspace><munder><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munder><mrow><mo minsize=\"1.2em\" maxsize=\"1.2em\">(</mo></mrow><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>−</mo><mi>n</mi><mrow><mo minsize=\"1.2em\" maxsize=\"1.2em\">)</mo></mrow><mo>⋅</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msup><mspace width=\"0.278em\"></mspace><mo>=</mo><mspace width=\"0.278em\"></mspace><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi></mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">[</mo><mo movablelimits=\"true\">gcd</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">]</mo><mo>,</mo></math></span></div>\n<p class=\"display-continue\"><em> where <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>:=</mo><munder><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo>∣</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></munder><mi>φ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>⋅</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>φ</mi><mo>∗</mo><mrow><mi>Id</mi></mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></math></span> is Pillai’s gcd-sum function <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><munder><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></munder><mo movablelimits=\"true\">gcd</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></math></span> <span\nclass=\"citation\" data-cites=\"toth-gcd\"><a href=\"papers/erdos249-totient-reasoning-surface.html#ref-15\">[15]</a></span> and <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Y</mi></math></span> are the independent fair-coin waiting\ntimes of Proposition <a class=\"math-ref\" href=\"papers/erdos249-totient-reasoning-surface.html#prop:coprime\" data-universe-ref=\"statement:erdos249-totient-reasoning-surface#prop:coprime\">5.9</a>. The identity itself\nis machine-checked; irrationality of <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi></mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">[</mo><mo movablelimits=\"true\">gcd</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">]</mo></math></span> is not proved here.\nThis is a different series from <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>S</mi></math></span>.</em></p>"]],"source":"erdos249-totient-reasoning-surface.json?v=e6abdbcd8877"}
